(Regression test: the canonical `a TYPE called NAME is VALUE.` declaration
 form must keep working unchanged alongside the newer `Create a TYPE
 called NAME.` default-initializing form - both now route through the
 same try_parse_type_noun resolver in src/parser/mod.rs. `file`'s is-form
 is declared only, not exercised further here - see the master report:
 a file declared through this generic path parses but is not registered
 in the analyzer's file_variables set, so property/read access on it
 (unlike a file opened with `Open a file ... called N.`) is rejected.)

A number called n is 41.
Print n.

A float called f is 2.5.
Print f.

A text called t is "hello".
Print t.

A boolean called b is yes.
Print b.

A list called l is [1, 2, 3].
Print l.

A map called m is {"k": 9}.
Print m.

A buffer called buf is "abc".
Print buf.

A value called v is 99.
Print v.

A time called clk is current time.
if clk is greater than 0, print "clk is set".

A file called src is "declare_create_is_form.vox".
Print "file declared ok".
